<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3419] Potential dependency conflict when the version of a dependency is changed on zeppelin interpreters</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3419</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Potential dependency conflict when the version of a dependency is changed on zeppelin interpreters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, if you have the dependency &quot;dependency:0.1&quot;, and you change the version to &quot;dependency:0.2&quot;, the old dependency does not get removed from the folder where zeppelin stores the dependencies jars, causing potential dependency conflicts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
